  "scope": "A common observer-stability and propagation cone conditionally fixes gapless dispersion. For the given canonical two-polarization Gaussian vacuum, a spherical cone fixes the free linear-wave Hamiltonian and its residue. The cubic Gaussian parent fails uniform tilted vacuum stability. Identical regional modular data alone cannot select the clock. No microscopic cone, finite-spin phase, full microcausality, nonlinear Einstein gravity, universal matter coupling, or TOE is proved. No Lean theorem."
